    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "These references demonstrate our ability to improve efficiency, quality of service, and access to information. To consolidate agent contributions into a coherent tender response, our will utilize our governance tools, such as the RAID log, Decision log, and Change request process, as well as our Steering committee. our dedicated change manager will ensure that all stakeholders are aligned and that the solution is designed to meet the client's needs. our will also apply our typical delivery structure, which includes phases like Inception & Design, Pilot / MVP, Full Rollout, and Operations & Support." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This approach will enable our to ensure continuity of processing of files and integrate the solution into existing practices. our reporting cadence, including Weekly status reports, Monthly steering committee meetings, and Quarterly executive reviews, will keep all stakeholders informed and aligned throughout the project. With our experience in managing large projects, including a largest project managed worth 4.5 million euros, our are confident in our ability to deliver a successful project that meets the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires a solution with times of response lower than 2 seconds for current requests (con10), high level of relevance of the answers (con11), and integration with existing system of information including business softwares and electronic management of documents (con13). The solution must also provide a high level of availability of the order of 99.9% (con12) and be designed as a tool of assistance with no automated decisions without explicit validation (con9). How can we design the technical architecture to meet these requirements, and what technology stack would you propose? To meet The client requirements, I would propose a technical architecture that leverages we expertise in AI/ML systems, Cloud architecture, API integration, Data engineering, and Cybersecurity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For the AI/ML component, we can utilize we experience with LLM models such as Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3, CamemBERT, or Falcon, which can provide a high level of relevance in answers. we can fine-tune LLM models such as Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3, CamemBERT, or Falcon using methods like LoRA, QLoRA, or Full fine-tune to achieve the desired performance. To ensure times of response lower than 2 seconds for current requests, we can deploy The solution on a cloud provider with low latency, such as OVHcloud, Scaleway, or Outscale (SecNumCloud), and utilize containerization using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) for efficient resource allocation. We can also use an inference server like vLLM, Ollama, or TGI (Hugging Face) to optimize the model's performance. For integration with existing systems of information, including business softwares and electronic management of documents, we can utilize API gateways like Kong, Apigee, or AWS API Gateway, and message brokers like Apache Kafka or RabbitMQ. we experience with GED systems such as Alfresco, Maarch Courrier, or OpenKM can also be leveraged for this purpose." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To achieve a high level of availability of the order of 99.9%, we can design the architecture to be highly available, using monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack to detect any issues promptly. we can also utilize we expertise in IAC tools like Terraform and Ansible to automate the deployment and management of the infrastructure. Finally, to ensure that The solution is designed as a tool of assistance with no automated decisions without explicit validation, we can implement explainability tools like SHAP, LIME, chain-of-thought prompting, or RAG source citation to provide transparency into the decision-making process. Overall, we proposed technical architecture would be based on a microservices design, leveraging cloud-native technologies and AI/ML expertise to meet the client's requirements. we can also ensure that the solution is secure, using security design patterns like Zero-trust, VLAN segmentation, mTLS between services, AES-256 at rest, and TLS 1.3 in transit, as well as secrets management tools like HashiCorp Vault or CyberArk Conjur." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (con5), hosting exclusively on the territory of the European Union (con6), no transfer of data outside the European Union (con7), and protection of sensitive data in an appropriate manner (con8). How can we ensure that we solution meets these regulatory requirements, and what security controls would you implement to guarantee the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the data? As a Security and Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. has experience with GDPR compliance, as indicated by the appointment of a Data Protection Officer (DPO) and the availability of a DPA template. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. standard data residency policy is the European Union only, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers outside the European Union unless there is an explicit legal basis. To ensure GDPR compliance, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. would implement the following security controls:  Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have ISO 27001 certification, which demonstrates Nexus Engineering S.r.l. commitment to information security management." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The scope of ISO 27001 certification, which demonstrates our commitment to information security management includes the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems. For data protection, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. utilize anonymization tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also have capabilities for implementing data subject rights, including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection. In terms of access control, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2). Role-based access control (RBAC) design is part of Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have worked with privileged access management (PAM) solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. network security architecture follows zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth patterns. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also deploy intrusion detection and prevention systems (IDS/IPS) and conduct regular penetration testing. To guarantee the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. log all queries, ensure log immutability using append-only methods with SHA-256 hash chaining, and retain audit logs for 7 years. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a security incident response team (SIRT) in place and conduct semi-annual drills to ensure preparedness. Given these capabilities and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience with regulatory frameworks like GDPR, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. are well-equipped to meet The tender requirements for strict GDPR compliance, hosting data exclusively within the European Union, not transferring data outside the European Union, and protecting sensitive data appropriately." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by the solution can be explained (req13) and that no decision will be automated without explicit validation of an agent (con9). the solution must also comply with regulatory requirements in force (con21) and respect the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) (con5). What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with these requirements? Based on we company context, we can identify some potential legal risks related to The client requirements. The requirement for explainability of recommendations or proposals issued by the solution (req13) and the constraint that no decision will be automated without explicit validation of an agent (con9) are aligned with we AI regulatory knowledge, specifically we expertise in EU AI Act and awareness of prohibited AI practices.  we have a policy of no automated decision-making without human validation, which complies with con9." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we expertise in transparency and explicability obligations for limited-risk AI systems can help address The requirement for explainability of recommendations or proposals issued by the solution (req13). Regarding compliance with regulatory requirements (con21) and the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) (con5), we have experience working with EU institutions and are aware of the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) (con5). we standard legal basis for processing personal data is Article 6(1)(e) – performance of task in public interest, and we have a data protection agreement template version 3.2. However, since our company context does not explicitly cover all aspects of explainability or automated decision-making validation mechanisms, it would be essential to conduct further analysis and ensure that we specific solution design meets all aspects of explainability or automated decision-making validation mechanisms. As for the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) (con5) compliance, given that we operations are intra-EU only and we do not require Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) or adequacy decisions, we should be able to comply with the client's expectations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nonetheless, we must carefully review we data processing practices to ensure our data processing practices meet all relevant the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) (con5) obligations, including those related to data protection by design and default. In terms of legal risks, we should flag potential issues related to AI transparency, explainability, and accountability, as well as the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) (con5) compliance, particularly regarding data subject rights, data breaches, and cross-border data transfers within EU.  we typical legal risks monitored include open-source license compliance, cross-border data flow (intra-EU only), EU AI Act compliance evolution, and vendor lock-in mitigation, which are partially relevant to the client's requirements but do not fully address the client's requirements. In conclusion, while we have some relevant expertise and policies in place, we need to carefully examine we specific solution design and implementation to ensure full compliance with the client's requirements and regulatory expectations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years (con16), and the annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority (con17). Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimization strategies our can propose to optimize costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected? Based on our context, our have a target gross margin percentage of 28 and a minimum acceptable margin percentage of 18." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To determine our projected margin on this contract, our need to estimate the total cost of the project. However, since our do not have information about the specific costs associated with the project, our can only provide general guidance. Assuming our can allocate resources efficiently and maintain our pricing model, our projected margin on this contract would likely be within our target range of 28% or above the minimum acceptable margin of 18%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To optimize costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected, our could propose cost-optimization strategies such as renegotiating rates with subcontractors if needed, as indicated in our budget reduction impact assessment. Additionally, our could explore options for reducing variable costs, which account for 65% of our project costs, and focus on process efficiencies to minimize the impact on the quality of service. our current financial position, with an equity of 1,450,000 euros and a debt-to-equity ratio of 0.42, suggests our have a stable foundation to take on the project. Furthermore, our credit line of 300,000 euros provides our with additional flexibility to manage cash flow if needed." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the client's emphasis on cost optimization (req16) and environmental considerations (con18, con19), our could also explore opportunities to reduce energetic consumption and propose solutions with low carbon impact, aligning with the client's requirements while maintaining our profitability goals." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution will have to provide intelligent assistance to agents in agents daily missions (req6), facilitate access to information (req3), improve the quality of answers (req4), and reduce times of processing (req5). How can we design an AI component that meets these requirements, and what innovation strategy would you propose to enhance the solution? To meet the client's requirements, I propose designing an AI component based on our existing capabilities in Large Language Models (LLMs) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). our preferred sovereign model, Mistral 7B Instruct, can be fine-tuned using our expertise in LoRA, QLoRA, or full fine-tuning on a domain-specific corpus to improve the quality of answers.  our can leverage our RAG capabilities, including dense vector retrieval and hybrid strategies, to facilitate access to information and provide relevant context to agents. leverage will enable the AI component to generate accurate and informative responses, reducing processing times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To enhance the solution, I propose an innovation strategy that builds on our current research topics, such as knowledge graphs for procedural reasoning and multi-agent collaboration frameworks. By integrating these concepts into the AI component, we can create a more comprehensive and adaptive system that learns from agent interactions and improves over time. Additionally, our experience with explainability methods like source citation, chain-of-thought display, and SHAP can be applied to provide transparent and trustworthy outputs, addressing the client's requirements for explicability and transparency." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our typical V1 to V2 development cycle of 9 months, I suggest a phased approach to deploying the AI component, with regular evaluations and fine-tuning to ensure the solution meets the client's evolving needs and constraints. This will also allow our to incorporate feedback from agents and stakeholders, further refining the AI component performance and usability. By combining our LLM and RAG expertise with a focused innovation strategy, we can create an intelligent assistance tool that effectively supports agents in agents daily missions while meeting the client's requirements for improved efficiency, quality, and reduced processing times." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of The City of Belval systems of information (req17) and reduce energetic consumption (con18). The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact (con19). What sustainability measures can we implement in we solution to meet these environmental requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet The City of Belval environmental requirements, we can implement several sustainability measures. Firstly, we can leverage we green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, which are both located in France and use 100% renewable energy. leverage aligns with the requirement to rely on infrastructures with low carbon impact. Additionally, we can apply digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation, which reduces GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%. we also employ auto-scaling to zero outside business hours and use query result caching, which is estimated to reduce recomputation by around 20%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Furthermore, we green IT hardware procurement policy ensures a minimum 5-year lifecycle for we equipment. By utilizing several sustainability measures and partnering with eco-friendly hosting providers, we can contribute to reducing the energetic consumption of its systems of information. we typical energy reduction versus baseline is around 35%, which can help minimize the environmental footprint of its systems of information." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval's digital transformation strategy aims to improve the efficiency of The City of Belval's administrative services and the quality of service rendered to users. To achieve improve, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposes a solution that leverages Nexus Engineering experience in managing public sector projects, particularly in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT. Nexus Engineering project management methodologies, including PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe, will ensure efficient delivery and integration into existing practices. a solution that leverages our experience in managing public sector projects, particularly in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT will provide an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents' work environment, capable of accompanying the agents' in the agents' administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents' work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities will bear on the search for information in internal procedures and applicable regulations, help with drafting letters or answers to users, accompaniment in the instruction of files, and suggestion of actions or steps to realize in an administrative process. Nexus Engineering technical architecture will utilize Large Language Models (LLMs) such as Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3, CamemBERT, or Falcon, which can provide a high level of relevance in answers. Nexus Engineering will fine-tune Large Language Models (LLMs) such as Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3, CamemBERT, or Falcon using methods like LoRA, QLoRA, or Full fine-tune to achieve the desired performance. a solution that leverages our experience in managing public sector projects, particularly in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT will be deployed on a cloud provider with low latency, such as OVHcloud, Scaleway, or Outscale (SecNumCloud), and utilize containerization using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) for efficient resource allocation. To ensure times of response lower than 2 seconds for current requests, Nexus Engineering will use an inference server like vLLM, Ollama, or TGI (Hugging Face) to optimize the model's performance. a solution that leverages our experience in managing public sector projects, particularly in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT will also integrate with existing systems of information, including business softwares and electronic management of documents, using API gateways like Kong, Apigee, or AWS API Gateway, and message brokers like Apache Kafka or RabbitMQ." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR), hosting data exclusively on the territory of the European Union, with no transfer of data outside the European Union authorized. Sensitive data will be protected in an appropriate manner using encryption, anonymization if necessary, and access control measures like multi-factor authentication (MFA) and role-based access control (RBAC). a solution that leverages our experience in managing public sector projects, particularly in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT will provide explainability into the decision-making process, using tools like SHAP, LIME, chain-of-thought prompting, or RAG source citation. Nexus Engineering will also ensure that no decision is automated without explicit validation of an agent, aligning with Nexus Engineering policy of no automated decision-making without human validation. a solution that leverages our experience in managing public sector projects, particularly in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT will be designed to meet the client's requirements for improved efficiency, quality, and reduced processing times. Nexus Engineering phased approach to deploying the AI component, with regular evaluations and fine-tuning, will ensure that a solution that leverages our experience in managing public sector projects, particularly in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT meets the client's evolving needs and constraints. Nexus Engineering will also implement several sustainability measures to reduce the energetic consumption of The City of Belval's systems of information. Nexus Engineering green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, use 100% renewable energy, and Nexus Engineering apply digital sobriety practices like INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, and query result caching." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering projected margin for this contract is expected to be within Nexus Engineering target range of 28% or above the minimum acceptable margin of 18%. Nexus Engineering will optimize costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected by renegotiating rates with subcontractors if needed, reducing variable costs, and focusing on process efficiencies. The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. Nexus Engineering annual cost of exploitation will remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. In conclusion, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposes a comprehensive solution that meets The City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence solution to assist agents in agents daily missions. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience in public sector projects, technical expertise, and commitment to sustainability make Nexus Engineering S.r.l. a suitable partner for the project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. are confident that a comprehensive solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence solution to assist agents in their daily missions will improve the efficiency of administrative services, enhance the quality of service rendered to users, and reduce processing times, while ensuring strict compliance with regulatory requirements and minimizing environmental impact." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing. The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3. Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained. It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents. To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7. Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8. Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the requirements to improve efficiency of administrative services, quality of service rendered to users, and facilitate access to information for agents (req1, req2, req3), as well as the need to integrate into existing practices (con1) and ensure continuity of processing of files (req9, con20), what are our project management methodologies and past public sector references that can be applied to meet these needs, and how will our consolidate all agent contributions into a coherent tender response? To address the client's requirements, our can leverage our experience in managing public sector projects, particularly in digital transformation, AI solutions, and public sector IT. our project management methodologies include PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe, which can be applied to ensure efficient delivery and integration into existing practices. our have completed 23 public sector projects, including a digital workplace transformation for the Comune di Torino, an AI-powered document management system for Regione Lombardia, and an intelligent citizen services platform for Métropole de Lyon." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

